MANUAL SCHEMA CREATION

I haven't figured out how to tell Django that these exist, so for now we
have to do manual migrations to create new schema.  To do this, in /django/desidb:

  python manage.py makemigrations everest --empty

replacing everest with the appropriate django ap.  That will create a
file in everest/migrations.  Edit that file to have:

    operations = [
       migrations.RunSQL(
         sql = f"CREATE USER desi PASSWORD {os.getenv('DESIPASSWORD')} LOGIN",
         reverse_sql = "DROP USER desi"
       )
       migrations.RunSQL( 
         sql = 'CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS everest',
         reverse_sql = 'DROP SCHEMA IF EXISTS everest'
       ),
       migrations.RunSQL(
         sql = 'GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA everest TO desi',
         reverse_sql = 'REVOKE USAGE ON SCHEMA everest FROM desi'
       )
       migrations.RunSQL(
         sql = ( 'ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA everest '
                 'GRANT SELECT ON TABLES TO desi' )
         reverse_sql = ( 'ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA everest '
                         'REVOKE SELECT ON TABLES FROM desi' )
      )
    ]

or whatever SQL you really need.  (Remember to add 'import os' at the
top.)  (For schema creation, only include the user creation in the *very*
first one.  Change everest, of course, to whatever the schema is.)


